* Mon Oct 19 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.2.4-1
- The generator makes random character passwords only, the word list is gone

* Mon Oct 19 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.2.3-1
- Start with search now opens the search field with the keyboard

* Mon Oct 19 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.2.2-1
- Ship the licenses of rnp and the EFF word list
- New icon

* Mon Oct 19 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.2.1-1
- Go back to the list when the key isn't unlocked

* Mon Oct 19 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.2.0-1
- Like pass, the first line is the password, other password: lines are fields
- Moving re-encrypts entries for the keys of their new folder
- Refuse symbolic links in the store
- Run git operations one at a time and undo a pull that conflicts
- Close an opened password after the set time and after deleting it
- Only give the git password to network operations for the remote's host
- Keep remembering the passphrase when set to until closed
- Safer keyring and SSH key writes, short key ids in .gpg-id
- Keep only hashes of recently used entries, forget deleted ones

* Mon Oct 19 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.1.5-1
- Keep the keyboard open while searching

* Mon Oct 19 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.1.4-1
- Pick an existing SSH private key for git
- Don't start cloning over ssh without a key
- Explain rejected SSH keys and keep long messages up longer

* Mon Oct 19 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.1.3-1
- Run ssh without a shell and allow it past the sandbox's ssh blacklist

* Mon Oct 19 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.1.2-1
- Let git, ssh and ssh-keygen run in the app's sandbox

* Mon Oct 19 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.1.1-1
- Import key files encrypted with a passphrase (gpg --symmetric)
- Count imported keys without their subkeys

* Mon Oct 19 2026 Joachim Klahr <klahr@r8.rs> 0.1.0-1
- First release: browse, search, decrypt, edit, move and delete entries,
  one-time codes, password generator, app-private OpenPGP keyring and
  git clone, pull, push and sync
